https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ue9UYWSX9hw  (Capo 0)

TIP:  There's a neat little riff that appears in the intro, outro, and between verses and is important to the song.  Fortunately it's not too hard to play but does require the proper attack.  Start with three strums of (C), then for the (Csus) roll your index finger down (or your whole hand over if you find you're coming up off the 4th and 5th strings) to cover the bottom sting of the 1st fret and strum, lift off the 1st string (or roll right) to return to (C) and strum.  Next comes the (Cadd9).  Keep your index finger of the (C) where it is and drop your free pinky straight down onto the 2nd string/3rd fret and strum, lift off to return to (C) and strum.  Repeat this sequence again.  Just try it a few times until you get a nice clean exchange and have the cadence down.  One strum per chord.

  
